---
title: "States"
description: "--<utility>--<state>: a value while the element is in that state."
section: Modifiers
sectionOrder: 2
order: 1
---

Color and effects utilities take a state tier: `--bg: var(--color-background); --bg--hover: var(--color-muted)`. A state beats a breakpoint on the same utility, and the states rank in a fixed order, highest first:

| State | Matches |
| --- | --- |
| `starting` | the element's `@starting-style`; see [starting](/api/modifiers/starting/) |
| `disabled` | `:disabled`, `[aria-disabled="true"]` |
| `active` | `:active` |
| `focus-visible` | `:focus-visible` |
| `focus-within` | `:focus-within` |
| `hover` | `:hover`, only where the device can hover |
| `checked` | `:checked`, `[aria-checked="true"]` |
| `current` | `[aria-current]` with any value but `"false"`: the current page, step, or location |
| `open` | `[open]`, `:popover-open`, `[aria-expanded="true"]` |
| `stuck` | the nearest sticky container is stuck; see [stuck](/api/modifiers/stuck/) |

Two consequences:

- **A tier needs a base.** `--text--hover: red` alone does nothing on a plain element; write the base first. The utilities that work tier-only (padding, `--bg`, opacity, the transforms, shadow and the ring utilities, and a handful of layout utilities with a natural default) are flagged in the [utility tables](/api/utilities/); `--bg--hover: var(--color-muted)` alone paints a plain element on hover. Where a primitive sets the property itself, its value wins over a tier alone unless the primitive reads that utility (a button reads `--bg`, a popover does not).
- **A utility on a primitive flattens its states.** `--bg: red` on a button is red on hover too, because the utility outranks the button's own `:hover` rule. To keep the primitive's behavior, set its state hook instead: `--ui-button-bg--hover`.
